<figure id="S4.T3" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="S4.T3.7" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 3</span>: </span><span id="S4.T3.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps" style="font-size:90%;">Mitra<span id="S4.T3.8.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_upright"> also demonstrates better performance with 1D attention model, showing that our priors are <em id="S4.T3.8.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">model-agnostic</em>. Winner/runner-up in shades of green <span id="S4.T3.8.1.2" class="ltx_text"></span>/ <span id="S4.T3.8.1.3" class="ltx_text"></span>.
The <math id="S4.T3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="95\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>95</mn><mo mathsize="1.110em">%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">95\%</annotation></semantics></math> confidence interval is shown in parentheses for the Elo. The columns in the aggregated metrics are mean and std (shown in parentheses) of the corresponding metric.
</span></span></figcaption>
