<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_figure"><a href="#S1.F1" title="Figure 1In Mitra: Mixed Synthetic Priors for Enhancing Tabular Foundation Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title">1
Mixture of priors in Mitra, Generalizability Matrix 
          
            G
          
         and Performance Vector 
          
            P
          
        .
We consider three factors for good priors: (1) the performance of a pretrained TFM using data generated solely from that prior on real tabular data (Point 1 and 
          
            P
          
        ); (2) its diversity and (3) distinctiveness when included in a mixture (Points 2 and 3, captured by the diagonal and off-diagonal entries of 
          
            G
          
        ). This leads to our mixture comprising SCM, gradient boosting, random forest and decision tree priors.
</span></a></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_figure"><a href="#S3.F2" title="Figure 2In 3 Mitra: TFM Pretrained on a Mixture of Priors ‣ Mitra: Mixed Synthetic Priors for Enhancing Tabular Foundation Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title">2Mitra Pipeline: Model agnostic visualized with either 1D or 2D attention.</span></a></li>
